1. The last micro‑batch’s forward must reach stage P: F(1, M-1) → F(2, M-1) → … → F(P, M-1). This takes at least P-1 time units after F(1, M-1) starts.
2. After F(P, M-1) finishes, the backward pass for micro‑batch M-1 must propagate back to stage 1: B_I(P, M-1) → B_I(P-1, M-1) → … → B_I(1, M-1). With overlapped communication, each step adds at least 1 time unit, giving another P-1 units.
3. Finally, B_W(1, M-1) (or any B_W that is on the critical path) must complete.

