Appendix F: Unified Optimality Theorem and Performance Bounds

F.1 Statement and Assembly

Theorem F.1 (Unified Optimality). Under the assumptions M \ge 2P-1, buffer credits \ge 2, and memory sufficient for the TopoMem plan, the combination of Stencil‑AD, AOP, and TopoMem yields a training iteration that is simultaneously correct (exact gradients), zero‑bubble, makespan‑minimal, and memory‑minimal among zero‑bubble schedules.

Proof. Directly follows from Theorems 3.1, 5.1, 5.3, and the optimality of TopoMem (D.2). ∎

F.2 MFU Bounds

Recalling the MFU formula (6.2):

MFU = \frac{T_{\text{comp}}}{T_{\text{comp}} + \bar{T}_{\text{bubble}} + \bar{T}_{\text{comm}}}.

· For AOP with M \ge 2P-1, \bar{T}_{\text{bubble}} = \frac{P-1}{3M} T_{\text{comp}} (since makespan = M T_{\text{comp}} + (P-1) in unit time and T_{\text{comp}} = 3).
· For 1F1B/GPipe, \bar{T}_{\text{bubble}} = \frac{P-1}{M} T_{\text{comp}}.
· Communication overhead \bar{T}_{\text{comm}} is bounded below by 2 S_{\text{act}} / BW if communication cannot be hidden. Thus the absolute ceiling is
  MFU_{\max} \le \frac{T_{\text{comp}}}{T_{\text{comp}} + \max(0,\, 2S_{\text{act}}/BW)}.

F.3 Memory‑Throughput Interplay

By TopoMem, the minimal memory under AOP is M_{\text{peak}} = P \cdot s_{\text{act}} (when no offloading is needed). If physical memory B_{\text{mem}} is smaller, TopoMem may resort to offloading, which consumes idle time; with sufficient idle time in the bubbles, this does not affect the schedule. If idle time is insufficient, the number of micro‑batches M may need to be reduced, which increases the bubble term. The joint optimisation of M and the memory plan is captured in Chapter 6.



