5. Why This Mix is Optimal

· C++ compiler uses STL, templates, and constexpr (for future compile‑time schedule evaluation) to perform heavy graph analysis cleanly.
· C runtime contains no C++ runtime dependencies, no exceptions, no RTTI, and can be compiled for bare‑metal accelerators or embedded devices.
· The boundary is exactly the generated source file, making the system auditable, portable, and mathematically transparent—in line with the dissertation’s philosophy.

This final code demonstrates the complete pipeline from theoretical BG‑IR to a static, optimal training binary, using the best tool for each half of the job.